\begin{quote}
\textbf{Introduction}

In today's rapidly evolving retail landscape, traditional store
management practices of-ten grapple with significant challenges,
including reliance on manual data collection, subjective
decision-making, and a notable absence of real-time insights into
customer behavior and op-erational efficiency. These limitations
frequently lead to financial losses, suboptimal resource allocation, and
missed opportunities to enhance the customer experience. The advent of
ad-vanced technologies, particularly in the fields of artificial
intelligence, computer vision, and data analytics, presents a
transformative opportunity to revolutionize in-store operations by
enabling precise, scalable, and responsive monitoring.

This report details the development of an \textbf{Intelligent Store
Monitoring and Ana-lytics System}, a comprehensive solution designed to
address these critical gaps. Undertaken as a Final Year Project at ISG
Tunis in collaboration with Copy Basta Agency, this project aims to
automate the observation and analysis of in-store activities, providing
store managers with actionable, data-driven insights. Our system
leverages cutting-edge computer vision mod-els, notably the YOLO (You
Only Look Once) architecture, for robust object detection and tracking,
alongside sophisticated data processing techniques to transform raw
video feeds into valuable business intelligence.

The project's development adhered to a dual-layered methodological
framework, combin-ing the agile principles of \textbf{Scrum} for overall
project management and the structured approach of \textbf{CRISP-DM
(Cross-Industry Standard Process for Data Mining)} for all data-centric
tasks. This synergistic methodology ensured iterative development,
continuous improvement, and a rigorous focus on data quality and model
performance.

Through this project, we aspire to empower store managers with an
unprecedented level of understanding of their retail environment,
enabling them to make informed decisions that optimize store layout,
enhance product placement, improve staff performance, and ultimately
drive profitability and customer satisfaction.

The report is structured to guide the reader through the project's
journey, starting with an in-depth \textbf{Project Study} that
introduces the host organization, Copy Basta, outlines the core problem,
and presents the adopted solution and methodologies. Following this, the
\textbf{State of the Art} chapter provides a foundational understanding
of the key technologies employed, in-cluding a detailed exploration of
computer vision, Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs), and the YOLO
model, as well as an introduction to Bird's Eye View mapping. Subsequent
chapters
\end{quote}

1

\begin{quote}
General Introduction

delve into the practical implementation through distinct development
sprints: \textbf{Sprint 0: Re-quirements Identification}, where the
functional and non-functional needs were meticulously defined;
\textbf{Sprint 1: Customer Demography Identification}, focusing on
developing models for gender classification; \textbf{Sprint 2: Customer
Activity Mapping in Store}, which details the creation of person
detection, tracking, BEV mapping, and heatmap generation capabilities;
and finally, the \textbf{Deployment} chapter, which describes the
development of the interactive user interface for presenting all
collected and analyzed insights.
\end{quote}

