\textbf{1.2} \textbf{Project Overview}

this project is presents for the framework of a Final Year Project in
ISG Tunis for the goal of obtaining of Business Computing Diplomat. The
Internship was performed with Copy Basta Agency.

\textbf{1.2.1} \textbf{Problematic}

Traditional store management relies on human decision-making and manual
data col-lection , which causes financial losses, inefficient resource
allocation and human errors. This approach lacks precision, scalability
and real-time responsiveness-critical factors in optimizing customer
experience and in-store operations.

With the advancement of Technologies such as data analytics, AI and
computer vision , which represents new opportunities to increase the
store monitoring activities observations performance. Yet the absence of
integration of intelligent monitoring tools prevents the ability of
stores to gain real-time , objective and scalable insights into the
internal operations.

This technical gap raises a critical question about how modern stores
can keep up with the digital transformation pace and customers
expectations with adapting technology to their management practices .

\textbf{1.2.2} \textbf{Solution Proposed}

Copy Basta Agency came with the idea of developing of an intelligent
store monitoring and analytics system powered by computer vision , AI
and data analytics . the goal is to automate the observation and
analysis of the in-store activities to provide a real-time insights
about the staff performance and the customers behavior. The system
includes major features
\end{quote}

