\begin{quote}
\textbf{1.3.2} \textbf{CRISP-DM Methodology}

CRISP-DM, which stands for Cross-Industry Standard Process for Data
Mining, is a structured framework designed to guide data mining efforts
within the field of data science {[}2{]}.

This cyclical methodology, employed by our data scientists, enables them
to operate in iterative phases: from gaining a deep understanding of the
client's business needs to the evaluation stage where results are
presented to clients, and finally to deployment. This approach offers a
systematic roadmap for data scientists throughout the entire project
lifecycle {[}2{]}.

\textbf{1.3.2.1 Business Understanding}

During this initial phase, the data science team collaborates closely
with stakeholders to grasp the project's business objectives, specific
requirements, limitations, and anticipated benefits {[}2{]}.

An assessment is conducted for the resources necessary to complete the
project, including budget allocations, required technical expertise, and
access to relevant data. The problems that need to be addressed are
identified, and clear criteria for measuring the project's success are
established {[}2{]}.

This foundational step is crucial for ensuring the successful
achievement of the project's goals {[}2{]}.
\end{quote}

