To ensure a structured, iterative, and efficient exécution of this
project, we propose to combine two complementary methodologies :
\textbf{Scrum} for project management and \textbf{CRISP-DM} for
data-related tasks.

\textbf{SCRUM :} the implementation of an Intelligent Store Monitoring
and Analytics System is a complex project with many features (customer
analysis, sellers tracking,heatmaps ..).Scrum is made for this kind of
projects for this reasons :

• Breaking the work into manageable sprints (between 1-4 weeks) allowing
incremental development and continuous improvement.

• Enabling frequent feesbacks ,adaptability for change and better
visiblity for all features.

• Maintaining organization and momentum through clearing roles
(development team,scrum master ,ect) and ceremonies(sprint planing ,
daily standups, sprint reviews ,ect)

\textbf{CRISP-DM :} for each sprint envolving data collection
,processing, or model training re-quires a structured approach to ensure
the quality and relevance of the models developed.CRISP-DM fits
perfectly beacuse :

• Providing a \textbf{standardized, step-by-step process} for data
science tasks.

• Guiding the team through \textbf{business understanding}, \textbf{data
preparation}, \textbf{modeling}, \textbf{evaluation}, and
\textbf{deployment}.

• Ensuring that the development of the model or data-driven features is
not rushed or misaligned with business objectives.

\textbf{A dual-layered framework:} refering to the integration of the
two methodologies :

• Scrum governs the overall planing of the project , task distribution
and process tracking.

• For any sprint involving AI modeling or data processing , the team
applies Crisp-dm to manage the data lifecycle and to ensure robust and
explainable results.

\textbf{Conclusion}

This chapter outlined our "Intelligent Store Monitoring and Analytics
System" project. We've shown how the project, in collaboration with
\textbf{Copy Basta}, aims to overcome the limita-tions of traditional
store management using \textbf{computer vision, AI, and data analytics}.
Our use of both \textbf{Scrum} and \textbf{CRISP-DM} ensures a robust
and adaptable approach to development.
\end{quote}

