\textbf{2.1.4.4 Pose Estimation}

The goal of pose estimation is to determine the position and orientation
of a person or object by predicting the location of key points, such as
hands, head, and elbows. This is particularly useful in applications
where understanding physical actions in real-time is impor-tant. Human
pose estimation is commonly used in areas like sports analysis, animal
behavior
\end{quote}

