\begin{quote}
Figure 2.8 shows a conceptual diagram of max pooling.

After an image has undergone multiple iterations of filtering
(convolution) and downsam-pling (max pooling), the outcome is a
compressed representation that encapsulates essential information about
the image. This representation is frequently fed into a dense network (a
standard neural network) to generate the ultimate output {[}4{]}.

\includegraphics[width=5.35417in,height=1.775in]{vertopal_8745fb96beba4c7f9cea35a5bfa22ab3/media/image17.png}
