working on an image

\begin{quote}
Figure 2.9 provides an example of how a convolutional network
effectively solves prob-lems. The model processes an image through
convolution and downsampling (max pooling) to create an abstract and
compact representation. This is then passed to a neural network for the
final output. The convolutional part of this model is often termed a
"backbone," while the final neural network is frequently referred to as
a "Head" {[}4{]}.
\end{quote}

