\textbf{Figure 2.16:} YOLO predictions

\begin{quote}
Figure 2.16 conceptually demonstrates YOLO predicting classes within
sub-regions of an image. If there are two classes (C=2, "dog" and "no
object") and the image is divided into 77 grid cells (S=7), YOLO's class
prediction output resembles the one shown, with all classes predicted
for each grid space. In practice, the actual output shape doesn't
strictly have to match this visual representation; it simply needs a
designated spot for each output. Thus, the final output for this model
would be a vector of length SSC. A model with this structure can
classify numerous regions within an image in a single pass {[}4{]}.
\end{quote}

