\textbf{Figure 2.18:} R-CNN bad predictions

\begin{quote}
Figure 2.18 illustrates what an inaccurate background detection might
look like. Because R-CNN cannot reason about the entire image (it only
processes small regions), it may generate arbitrary bounding boxes that
lack contextual relevance within the image {[}4{]}.

CNNs possess a "perceptive field," meaning that individual CNNs
inherently face a similar challenge: a specific point within a CNN can
only "see" a small portion of the input image. Theoretically, this might
lead YOLO to also make suboptimal prediction choices {[}4{]}.
\end{quote}

