\textbf{2.4.4} \textbf{Implementation Steps}

\textbf{2.4.4.1 Setup}

Start by calibrating the camera to acquire its intrinsic and extrinsic
parameters. This is typically accomplished using a chessboard
calibration method. The known geometric properties of the chessboard
provide a reliable reference, enabling the system to accurately compute
the necessary camera parameters {[}5{]}.

\textbf{2.4.4.2 Key points Detection}

Next, identify significant points (such as corners, edges, or road
markings) in both the initial camera view and the desired top-down BEV
plane. Establishing accurate correspon-dences between these points is
vital for calculating the homography matrix that will perform the
perspective transformation {[}5{]}.
\end{quote}

34

