\textbf{3.4} \textbf{Workspace Environment}

\textbf{3.4.1} \textbf{Software architecture}

\textbf{3.4.1.1 Environments}

• VS Code: is a source code editor and integrated development
environment ( IDE ) from Microsoft. It is open-source and
cross-platform, meaning it runs on Windows, Linux, and Mac. It was
designed for web developers, but it supports many other programming
languages such as C++, C\#, Python, Java, etc. It offers many features
like syntax highlighting, auto-completion, error highlighting, code
navigation, debugging, version control, integration with Git , and many
more. It is also extensible using a wide variety of community-developed
extensions, allowing developers to customize the editor according to
their needs{[}6{]}.

• Google Collab: Google Colab, short for Google Colaboratory , is a free
platform offered by Google that allows you to write and run Python code
in your browser. It allows you to run Jupyter notebooks without having
to worry about your hardware or software
\end{quote}

44

\begin{quote}
Chapter 3. Sprint 0 - Requirements identification

installed on your computer. Google Colab is a tool that also facilitates
access to computing resources and common machine learning libraries
{[}7{]}.

• Roboflow: is a web-based tool that helps users build, manage, and
deploy computer vision models without needing extensive machine learning
expertise. It provides an end-to-end pipeline for image-based AI
projects---from uploading and annotating datasets, to preprocessing
images, training models using various architectures, and deploying them
to different environments (web, mobile, edge devices, etc.).

\textbf{3.4.1.2 Programming Languages}

• Python: is a general-purpose computer programming language . Unlike
HTML, CSS, or JavaScript, its use is not limited to web development. It
can be used for any type of programming and software development.

It is used in particular for the back-end development of web or mobile
applications, and for the development of software and applications for
PCs. It also allows you to write system scripts, in order to create
instructions for a computer system.

Furthermore, Python is the most popular computer language for processing
Big Data , performing mathematical calculations , or Machine Learning .
Generally speaking, it is the preferred for Data Science.
\end{quote}

