OpenCV (Open Source Computer Vision Library) is a free and open-source
software library for computer vision and machine learn-ing,providing a
common infrastructure for computer vision applica-tions and accelerating
the use of machine perception in commercial products. As an Apache 2
licensed product, OpenCV allows busi-nesses to freely use and modify its
code; it includes over 2500 op-timized algorithms covering both classic
and advanced computer vision and machine learning techniques, enabling
functionalities such as face detection and recognition, object
identification, hu-man action classification in videos, camera and
object tracking, 3D modeling, image stitching, red-eye removal, eye
tracking, and aug-mented reality, making it widely used in industry,
academia, and government. {[}8{]}.
\end{quote}
\end{minipage} \\
\begin{minipage}[t]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\begin{quote}
Supervision
\end{quote}
\end{minipage} & \begin{minipage}[t]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\begin{quote}
Supervision is an open-source Python library developed by Roboflow. It
provides a high-level interface for handling post-processing,
visualization, and deployment of computer vision model outputs. The
library simplifies workflows after inference by offer-ing tools to
filter, manipulate, and display outputs like bounding boxes, class
labels, confidence scores, and segmentation masks. Supervision supports
popular frameworks such as YOLOv5, YOLOv8, and OpenCV, and enables
real-time image and video annotation. It is particularly effective for
model evaluation, debug-ging, and production deployment.
\end{quote}
\end{minipage} \\
\begin{minipage}[t]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\begin{quote}
Ultralytics
\end{quote}
\end{minipage} & \begin{minipage}[t]{\linewidth}\raggedright
\begin{quote}
Ultralytics is an open-source Python library that facilitates the
de-velopment, training, and deployment of advanced computer vision
models, especially the YOLO (You Only Look Once) family, includ-ing
YOLOv12. It supports tasks such as object detection, image
classification, segmentation, and pose estimation.

The library provides an intuitive API, pre-trained models, and
com-patibility with custom datasets. It supports real-time inference,
model export to various formats (e.g., ONNX, TensorRT), and ad-heres to
standard dataset formats, making it suitable for a wide range of
applications.
\end{quote}
\end{minipage} \\
\bottomrule()
\end{longtable}

