There are two primary approaches to labeling a dataset: manual
annotation, where each object is individually labeled by a human
annotator, and automatic annotation, which utilizes pre-trained models
to generate labels.

In this project, we employed manual annotation to ensure accuracy and
precision. Once the images were labeled, they were added to the
annotated dataset for subsequent training and evaluation phases.

